      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T21:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this function should only say if you are a foregroundUser or not.\n\nThen if we want to allow specific process, it should not be done inside this method but on a parallele call.\nSomething like:\n```\ncheckIfCallerIsForegroundUser() || checkIfCallerIsExceptionnallyAllowed()\n```\n\nBecause we have the checkBluetoothPermissions that looks on\n```\n if (isCallerSystem(callingAppId)) return true;\n        if (isCallerShell(callingAppId)) return true;\n        if (isCallerRoot(callingAppId)) return true;\n```\nbut here we are looking on \n```\n|| isCallerNfc(callingAppId)\n                        || isCallerSystemUi(callingAppId)\n                        || isCallerShell(callingAppId);\n```\n\nAnd both of theses looks like hidden bypass that I would like to make it obvious",
      "parentUuid": "2d755193_4912e7ea",
